    },
    {
      "id": "block_10",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        450,
        900,
        490
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_10",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "概括地说, 把一些确定的对象的全体叫做集合(set), 简称集. 集合通常用大写字母 $A$、$B$、$C$……表示."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_11",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        490,
        900,
        540
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_11",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "集合所含的各个对象叫做该集合的元素(element). 元素通常用小写字母 $a$、$b$、$c$……表示."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_12",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        540,
        900,
        610
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_12",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "如果 $a$ 是集合 $A$ 的元素, 就记作 $a \\in A$, 读作“$a$ 属于 $A$”; 如果 $a$ 不是集合 $A$ 的元素, 就记作 $a \\notin A$, 读作“$a$ 不属于 $A$”. 例如, 若 $A$ 是由数 1、3、5、7、9 组成的集合, 则 $1 \\in A$, $2 \\notin A$."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_13",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        610,
        900,
        690
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_13",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "集合的元素是确定的. 也就是说, 给定一个集合, 一个对象在不在这个集合中就确定了. 例如, “我国的直辖市”组成一个集合, 北京、上海、天津、重庆在这个集合中, 而杭州、南京、深圳等城市不在这个集合中."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_14",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        690,
        900,
        760
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_14",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "一些不确定的对象不能组成一个集合. 例如, “我们班里高个子的同学”不能组成一个集合. 因为“高个子”的标准不够明确、具体, 所以“我们班里高个子的同学”是不确定的."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_15",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        760,
        900,
        800
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_15",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "一个给定集合中的各个元素是互不相同的, 即一个元素在同一个集合中是不能重复出现的."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_16",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        800,
        900,
        850
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_16",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "如果两个集合 $A$ 与 $B$ 的组成元素完全相同, 就称这两个集合相等, 记作 $A=B$."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block_17",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "body",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        850,
        850,
        870
      ],
      "anchor_id": "block_17",
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "元素个数有限的集合称为有限集, 否则就称为无限集."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
